/T (hospital emergency waiting list. It registers patients, records basic details, assigns an urgency category, displays waiting patients, searches by patient ID, serves the next patient, and reports queue statistics. It demonstrates how a priority-based queue can order patients by urgency while preserving arrival order among patients with equal priority. Important: This is an educational simulation only. In real healthcare, urgency must be assessed by qualified clinical staff using approved triage procedures. This program must not be used to make medical decisions.)
/E (hospital emergency waiting list. It registers patients, records basic details, assigns an urgency category, displays waiting patients, searches by patient ID, serves the next patient, and reports queue statistics. It demonstrates how a priority-based queue can order patients by urgency while preserving arrival order among patients with equal priority. Important: This is an educational simulation only. In real healthcare, urgency must be assessed by qualified clinical staff using approved triage procedures. This program must not be used to make medical decisions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [34]
